Passthrough: network auto-detect without device redirection.

At 3.33.1, freerdp_client_load_addins turns DeviceRedirection on (so it asks for
rdpdr) whenever NetworkAutoDetect is on. Auto-detect (bandwidth and round-trip
measurement, MS-RDPBCGR 2.2.14) runs on the main channel and needs no rdpdr,
which this build leaves out; with it forced on, PreConnect fails. Without it,
Windows can measure the link and fit its H.264 to a slow one (a relay).

--- a/client/common/cmdline.c	2026-11-10 03:23:35
+++ b/client/common/cmdline.c	2026-11-22 17:11:49
@@ -6512,8 +6512,9 @@
 			return FALSE;
 	}
 
-	if (freerdp_settings_get_bool(settings, FreeRDP_NetworkAutoDetect) ||
-	    freerdp_settings_get_bool(settings, FreeRDP_SupportHeartbeatPdu) ||
+	/* Passthrough: network auto-detect runs on the main channel and needs no device redirection, which this
+	 * build doesn't compile in; only the heartbeat and multitransport still ask for it. */
+	if (freerdp_settings_get_bool(settings, FreeRDP_SupportHeartbeatPdu) ||
 	    freerdp_settings_get_bool(settings, FreeRDP_SupportMultitransport))
 	{
 		if (!freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_DeviceRedirection, TRUE))
